PyJWT==2.15.1
# bcrypt is called directly (passlib was dropped: unmaintained, and its
# bcrypt backend broke against bcrypt 5). bcrypt 5 enforces the 72-byte input
# limit natively — it raises instead of silently truncating — and the auth
# layer length-checks passwords before hashing.
